# AD Brain

Which airworthiness directives (ADs) apply to each aircraft, which were superseded, who decided
what and why, and what is still unknown. Every answer cites the exact sentence of the source.

**Status:** being built today at the KVA hackathon "AI brain for industry" (Turin, 14 Nov 2026).
The application code is written during the event.

**Prepared before the event** (rule 7; full list in `docs/PREPARED.md`): the dataset in `data/`,
the API contract (spec only) and the coding-assistant configuration.

**Data:** 21 real ADs (EASA, and FAA ADs as republished by EASA; texts in `data/raw/ads/`,
sources in `data/raw/ads/SOURCES.csv`), 3 real EU-registered aircraft (IAA Ireland register,
September 2025 snapshot, no owner data) and a synthetic flight-school fleet labelled `DEMO-xx`.

Team: Paparella & Raimondi.